From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] compare monitor HAL header storage with valid descriptor FC

0024 got 444 valid monitor descriptors including 20 Action types, and 444
post-restitch frames but zero post-restitch Actions. Counts do not prove those
Actions are AWDL, and equal input/output counts do not demonstrate packet loss.
Compare the existing HAL header pointer with metadata frame control, count
exact AWDL signatures there and within the bounded monitor descriptor region,
and log layout/tag values for at most eight Action descriptors. This reads
metadata already used by the restitch routines, never selects a new packet
header or changes reconstruction. No payload logging, packet-fate changes or
radio settings. Missing/out-of-bounds header storage is reported explicitly.

